  "Id": 1937,
  "Title": "The Open Islamicate Texts Initiative Arabic-script OCR Catalyst Project (OpenITI AOCP)",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "CorpusBuilder, OpenITI\u2019s digitization platform, will now be transformed into a full digital text production pipeline, thanks to a new grant from the Mellon Foundation",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass1B94FE8A04F9479CACC50417DE43367F\"><p>\u200bAKU-ISMC is delighted to announce that the Open Islamicate Texts Initiative, of which Professor Sarah Bowen Savant is a co-Principal Investigator, has received a grant of $800,000 from Mellon Foundation for the development of a digital text production pipeline for Persian and Arabic that will incorporate a wide range of new OCR enhancements. This grant will help to expand the number and range of Arabic and Persian texts that are in machine-readable format, and so greatly aid in research using digital methods.&#160;</p><p>For further information, please click <a href=\"https&#58;//medium.com/%40openiti/openiti-aocp-9802865a6586\">here\u200b</a>.</p></div>",
